{
  "comment": [
    "D-SINK-19 round 10, R20a (D-SRC-20): THE HELPER KEEPS WHAT THE SERVICE WRITES.",
    "Run by BOTH tests/Model.test.js and tests/test_state.py (CLAUDE.md: a rule written",
    "in two languages gets one fixture; the savedSearches precedent).",
    "",
    "`keys` is the whole vocabulary of state.json: every key the SERVICE can serialise",
    "(top level, per source record, and inside the nested records), each one the helper's",
    "normalize_state preserves. The node suite drives every model reducer Service.qml hands",
    "the state to, collects every key the results carry, and requires that set to EQUAL",
    "keys + serviceOnly; the python suite requires normalize_state over `document` to emit",
    "exactly `keys` + helperOnly. So a key added to either reader alone is red the day it is",
    "added. `serviceOnly` / `helperOnly` name a key one side writes and the other",
    "deliberately does not, each with its reason; both are empty today.",
    "",
    "`cases` pin the three keys round 9 and 10 added, value by value, through both readers:",
    "validated, never invented."
  ],
